code/method_plan.md is stamped 2026-07-22T11:36:53Z and says it was written before any calibration or cascade run. It declares all five required items:
- the switch form (Sec. 1, with pre-cascade refinements in Sec. 5bis and Sec. 7, each dated before any cascade and with the principle stated as unchanged);
- the selection principle (Sec. 1d);
- the lambda calibration: a 21-point blend sweep at the Te=0.1 eV reference with NotConverged excluded (Sec. 2);
- the recoil/stability sweep: {1,2,5,10,15,20} keV, N target 12 with a floor of 8, using the paper's >25% rule (Sec. 4);
- the baseline T* values: 0.5, 1.25, 2.5, 5.0 eV with sigma=T*/14, converted to K (Sec. 4).

codebase_notes.md documents what was inspected and reused:
- LAMMPS/ML-PACE: the per-atom hybrid/scaled scale field was inspected and reused unmodified;
- FitSNAP: the VASP2JSON/JSON format was inspected and not used to refit;
- DAKOTA: inspected and deliberately not used;
- OVITO: the modifiers used;
- what the agent implemented itself.

The function is derivative-continuous:
- softplus is C-infinity and strictly positive, so sqrt(kappa*softplus) is smooth;
- the clamp at x=1 is C1, because n>1 makes the slope n(1-x)^(n-1) go to 0;
- the maximum slope is finite (1.4e-4 per K).

The equilibrium response is negligible:
- lambda is at most 0.002 up to 1600 K;
- in the logged cascades during the 1000 K anneal, the maximum per-atom lambda is about 0.0015.
No atom is moved onto U_ht by equilibrium fluctuations. Caveat: the equilibrium local-T distribution behind T_thr is an analytic estimate (source 'analytic'); the measurement log stops at step 0.

No concrete regime where the final switch fails is identified with data. Failure signals in the submission's own data go unremarked:
- the energy error at the calibrated lambda=0.35 exceeds the sigmoid-implied point (55.5 vs 49.5 meV/atom);
- spike volume exceeds ground-state at 2 keV;
- there is no stability advantage at 1-5 keV.
Behavior above 5 keV is framed only as untested.

